    "title": "'Sense of stability': Durham provides hotels for people living in homeless encampment at Oakwood Park - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Hannah Leyva ,\n3 hours ago DURHAM, N.C. (WNCN) — A homeless encampment at Durham’s Oakwood Park is gone after city workers provided the people living there with temporary shelter. The city’s Community Safety Department told CBS 17 they successfully connected all 18 people with transportation and hotels that cost between $60 to $80 a night. Read full article\n3",
